# Agent Chat

Complete reference for inter-agent communication via `holly chat`.

mechanics, protocol, and coordination patterns.

See also: `ax-commandments` skill for mandatory tool design rules.

---

## Prerequisites

`HOLLY_SESSION_ID` must already be set in your environment (e.g.
`agent-<uuid>` or an existing `sess-XXXXXX`). Session identity is owned by the
shell/runtime and is read-only to Holly commands. The chat script injects this
into every message automatically. You do not need to include your session ID in
message bodies.

Verify: `echo $HOLLY_SESSION_ID` -- should print `agent-<uuid>` or `sess-XXXXXX`.

If unset, stop immediately. Do not use Holly lifecycle commands to manufacture
identity. Fix the shell/runtime bootstrap first. If the hook reports an
unclaimed VS Code UUID after the ID is present, run the exact `holly session
...` command it prints.

