## File-Based Posting Protocol

For anything beyond a simple ASCII line, use this protocol:

1. Create a sanctioned scratch directory with `agent-fs` and write the
   message body there:

```bash
scratch_dir="$(agent-fs scratch chat)"
create_file "$scratch_dir/chat_<channel>_<description>.txt"
```

2. Post with `--file`:

```bash
holly chat post --channel <channel> --file "$scratch_dir/chat_<channel>_<description>.txt"
```

**Why:** The `--message` flag passes through zsh, which mangles
quotes, special characters, and multi-line content. The file-based
protocol bypasses shell parsing entirely.

**Naming convention:** `$scratch_dir/chat_<channel>_<brief-description>.txt`

